\subsubsection{Health check}

[[pyalex]] hides HTTP status codes behind its own exceptions, so the probe
goes straight to the REST endpoint with [[requests]].  The email is not a
credential---OpenAlex accepts requests without one---so a 403 here is never a
\enquote{key rejected}; we pass [[authenticated=False]].  We do forward the
configured [[mailto]] so the probe exercises the same (polite) request pool
as real searches.

