\section{arXiv Provider}
\label{sec:arxiv}

arXiv is an open-access repository of electronic preprints, primarily in
physics, mathematics, computer science, quantitative biology, quantitative
finance, and statistics.
With over 2 million papers, it is the largest preprint server in the world.

\subsection{Package Choice}

We use the [[arxiv]] Python package, which provides a clean interface to the
arXiv API.
Like [[pyalex]] for OpenAlex, this package handles pagination and rate limiting
internally, simplifying our implementation.

\subsection{Authentication}

No API key is required---arXiv is fully open access.
This makes the provider always available.

\subsection{Rate Limiting and Retry}

arXiv's terms of use request no more than one request every three seconds.
The [[arxiv]] package respects this limit by default with its
[[delay_seconds]] parameter.

However, the arXiv API occasionally returns HTTP 500 errors.
We implement our own retry logic with exponential backoff to handle transient
failures.
Importantly, we only cache successful results---if a request fails, the cache
is not populated, allowing the user to retry immediately.

\subsection{Limitations}

arXiv does not provide citation or reference data through its API.
The [[get_paper_citations]] and [[get_paper_references]] methods raise
[[NotImplementedError]].
For citation data on arXiv papers, use Semantic Scholar or OpenAlex instead,
which index arXiv papers and provide citation graphs.

\subsection{Provider implementation}

