\subsubsection{DOI lookup}

For metadata enrichment, we support looking up arXiv papers via the canonical
arXiv DOI format [[10.48550/arXiv.<id>]].

arXiv's API does not provide a general DOI lookup, so we only handle this DOI
family by converting it back to an arXiv identifier and querying arXiv by ID.

<<arxiv get paper by doi>>=
def get_paper_by_doi(self, doi: str | None) -> Paper | None:
    """Fetch a single arXiv paper by its arXiv DOI."""
    if not doi:
        return None

    doi_str = doi.strip()
    cache_key = ("doi", doi_str)
    if cache_key in self._cache:
        logger.debug(f"arxiv: Cache hit for DOI {doi_str}")
        return self._cache[cache_key]

    doi_lc = doi_str.lower()
    prefix = "10.48550/arxiv."
    if not doi_lc.startswith(prefix):
        self._cache[cache_key] = None
        return None

    arxiv_id = doi_str[len("10.48550/arXiv.") :].strip()
    if not arxiv_id:
        self._cache[cache_key] = None
        return None

    try:
        search = arxiv.Search(id_list=[arxiv_id], max_results=1)
        for result in self._client.results(search):
            converted = self._convert_result(result)
            # Ensure the DOI matches the lookup DOI for merge_with equality.
            paper = Paper(
                title=converted.title,
                authors=converted.authors,
                year=converted.year,
                doi=doi_str,
                abstract=converted.abstract,
                venue=converted.venue,
                url=converted.url,
                pdf_url=converted.pdf_url,
                citation_count=converted.citation_count,
                keywords=converted.keywords,
                tags=converted.tags,
                sources=converted.sources,
                references=converted.references,
                citations=converted.citations,
            )
            self._cache[cache_key] = paper
            return paper

        self._cache[cache_key] = None
        return None
    except Exception as e:
        logger.warning("arxiv: DOI lookup failed: %s", e)
        return None
@

\subsubsection{Retry with exponential backoff}

We implement our own retry logic since the [[arxiv]] package's built-in
retry may not handle all transient failures (especially HTTP 500 errors).
The backoff starts at 3 seconds and doubles with each attempt.

Importantly, we only cache successful results.
If a request fails after all retries, we return an empty list without caching,
allowing the user to retry immediately.

<<arxiv search with retry>>=
last_exception: Exception | None = None

for attempt in range(self.MAX_RETRIES):
    try:
        all_papers: list[Paper] = []
        for result in self._client.results(search):
            paper = self._convert_result(result)
            <<arxiv apply year filter>>
            all_papers.append(paper)

        logger.debug(f"arxiv: Retrieved {len(all_papers)} papers")

        # Only cache successful results
        if all_papers:
            self._cache[cache_key] = all_papers

        return all_papers

    except (arxiv.HTTPError, arxiv.UnexpectedEmptyPageError) as e:
        last_exception = e
        if attempt < self.MAX_RETRIES - 1:
            backoff = self.INITIAL_BACKOFF * (2 ** attempt)
            logger.warning(
                "arxiv: %s (attempt %d/%d, retrying in %.1fs)",
                e, attempt + 1, self.MAX_RETRIES, backoff
            )
            time.sleep(backoff)
        else:
            logger.warning(
                "arxiv: %s (attempt %d/%d, giving up)",
                e, attempt + 1, self.MAX_RETRIES
            )

    except Exception as e:
        # Non-retryable error
        logger.warning("arxiv: %s", e)
        return []

# All retries exhausted
return []
@

\subsubsection{Applying filters}

arXiv supports category filtering via its query syntax.
For year filtering, we apply client-side filtering since arXiv does not
support date range queries natively.

<<arxiv apply filters>>=
if filters:
    # Category/venue filter: use arXiv category syntax
    if filters.venue:
        # User may specify "cs.AI" or just "cs"
        effective_query = f"cat:{filters.venue} AND ({query})"

    # Open access filter: arXiv is always open access
    if filters.open_access:
        logger.debug("arxiv: All papers are open access, filter has no effect")

    # Publication types: arXiv only has preprints
    if filters.pub_types:
        # Only proceed if "preprint" is in the requested types
        if not any(pt.lower() == "preprint" for pt in filters.pub_types):
            logger.warning(
                "arxiv: Only preprints available, but requested types: %s",
                filters.pub_types
            )

    # Minimum citations: not supported
    if filters.min_citations is not None:
        logger.warning("arxiv: Citation filtering not supported")
